pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% The `<=` half of `reification_right_implication_negative_degree`: the big-M
% coefficient there is `sum - degree`, and `x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 <= 5` (a tautology,
% since x1 is 0/1) was stored as the real constraint `1 ~x1 4 x2 4 x3 >= 4`.
f 1 ;
e x2 x3 ==> 1 x1 <= 5 : 1 ;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
